{"kind":"text","seq":49,"text":"Round 2 done. Four builds, four tested circuits (6.44 → 2.03 → 6.59 → **6.65**).\n\nKey finding this round: intensity ≥10 triggers a hard excitement penalty. Build #2 had the *highest* raw excitement (~8.1) but intensity 14.47 slashed it to 2.03. Everything after that was intensity management: an L-shaped chain lift (freed map room so turns could be placed at hill crests where the train is slow), a softer 60° pullout, and banked-only turns dropped max lateral G from 3.24→2.86 and positive G from 5.55→4.78, landing intensity at 9.52 — just under the cliff.\n\n**Best: 86-piece steel twister — L-shaped 40 ft chain lift, 32 ft plunge into a vertical loop, then a serpentine of airtime hops threaded with three corkscrew pairs across two lanes; excitement 6.65, intensity 9.52, nausea 5.77, 4 inversions, 10 drops, 74 air time, similarity 0.40.**"}
